A growable sequence of values of one type.

Use alloc and core.

A public record List of T has a data as a pointer to T, a len as an unsigned number, and a cap as an unsigned number.

Publicly, to create_list for T, named list_new, returning List of T.
created is List of T.
Give back created.

Publicly, to push for T given items as a pointer to List of T, val as T, named list_push, returning nothing.
Call this as "push <val> to <items>".
Call this as "append <val> to <items>".
If items's len equals items's cap.
Let new_cap be items's cap times 2.
If items's cap equals 0, make new_cap 8 as an unsigned number.
If new_cap is less than 16, make new_cap 16 as an unsigned number.
Let old_bytes be items's cap times (byte size of T).
Let new_bytes be new_cap times (byte size of T).
Let resized be resize memory at items's data as a pointer to byte from old_bytes to new_bytes.
Set items's data to resized as a pointer to T.
Set items's cap to new_cap.
End the condition.
Set item items's len of items's data to val.
Add 1 to items's len.

Publicly, to pop for T given items as a pointer to List of T, named list_pop, returning T.
Call this as "pop from <items>".
If items's len equals 0, stop with error "pop from empty list".
Set items's len to items's len minus 1.
Give back item items's len of items's data.

Publicly, to get_item for T given items as a pointer to List of T, index as an unsigned number, named list_get, returning T.
If index is at least items's len, stop with error "list index out of bounds".
Give back item index of items's data.

Publicly, to set_item for T given items as a pointer to List of T, index as an unsigned number, val as T, named list_set, returning nothing.
If index is at least items's len, stop with error "list index out of bounds".
Set item index of items's data to val.

Publicly, to count_list for T given items as a pointer to List of T, named list_len, returning an unsigned number.
Call this as "count of <items>".
Give back items's len.

Publicly, to first_item for T given items as a pointer to List of T, named list_first, returning T.
Call this as "first item of <items>".
If items's len equals 0, stop with error "first item of empty list".
Give back item 0 of items's data.

Publicly, to last_item for T given items as a pointer to List of T, named list_last, returning T.
Call this as "last item of <items>".
If items's len equals 0, stop with error "last item of empty list".
Give back item (items's len minus 1) of items's data.

Publicly, to clear_list for T given items as a pointer to List of T, named list_clear, returning nothing.
Call this as "clear <items>".
Set items's len to 0 as an unsigned number.

Publicly, to free_list for T given items as a pointer to List of T, named list_free, returning nothing.
Call this as "free <items>".
If items's data is not empty, release memory at items's data as a pointer to byte.
Set items's data to no address as a pointer to T.
Set items's len to 0 as an unsigned number.
Set items's cap to 0 as an unsigned number.

Publicly, to sort_list for T given items as a pointer to List of T, compare as a function taking pointer to T and pointer to T returning whole number, named list_sort, returning nothing.
Call this as "sort <items> using <compare>".
Let outer be 0 as an unsigned number.
While outer is less than items's len.
Let inner be outer.
While inner is more than 0.
Let left be address of item (inner minus 1) of items's data.
Let right be address of item inner of items's data.
If apply compare to right with left is less than 0, let temporary be item inner of items's data, set item inner of items's data to item (inner minus 1) of items's data, set item (inner minus 1) of items's data to temporary, set inner to inner minus 1, otherwise break.
End the loop.
Add 1 to outer.
End the loop.
